## 3.9 Relationships

### Purpose

The Relationships section documents the engineering relationships between a System Objective and other approved objectives within the AVIA repository.

Its purpose is to preserve dependency, hierarchy, and interaction information, enabling engineers to understand how objectives collectively contribute to the overall system architecture.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Parent Objective(s) | Higher-level objective(s) from which this objective is derived, where applicable. |
| Child Objective(s) | Lower-level objective(s) derived from this objective, where applicable. |
| Supporting Objective(s) | Objectives that contribute to achieving this objective. |
| Dependent Objective(s) | Objectives that depend on this objective for successful achievement. |
| Related Objective(s) | Other objectives with significant engineering relationships. |

---

### Relationship Rules

Relationships shall:

- Reference only approved System Objectives.
- Be supported by engineering justification where required.
- Maintain bidirectional consistency where applicable.
- Be reviewed whenever related objectives are added, revised, or retired.
- Preserve traceability across the objective network.

---

### Engineering Note

Relationships describe engineering connections between objectives.

They do not establish governance authority or ownership, which are defined separately within the governance framework.
